": [\"Rashmi Icon\", \"Rashmi Avenue\", \"Rashmi Vasudeo\", \"Rashmi Celestia\"]}","promises":[],"promises_total":0,"promoters":[{"name":"Dineshkumar C. Modi (Dinesh Modi)","role":"Chairman & Managing Director (DIN: 02793201); disclosed as a Director and Key Managerial Personnel related party"},{"name":"Mahek Dineshkumar Modi","role":"Whole-Time Director & Chief Financial Officer; disclosed as Key Managerial Personnel related party"},{"name":"Rashmi Dineshkumar Modi","role":"Whole Time Director; disclosed as Key Managerial Personnel related party"}],"related":"[{\"name\": \"Modis Navnirman Foundation\", \"relation\": \"subsidiary\", \"note\": \"Subsidiary since 20-01-2026 per Form AOC-1; reporting period same as the holding company (April 1, 2025 to March 31, 2026); reporting currency Indian Rupees, not a foreign subsidiary. Extent of shareholding stated as …","risks":[{"note":"The auditors state that redevelopment projects are exposed to risks relating to regulatory approvals, which may significantly impact the recoverability and valuation of inventory. Audit procedures included reviewing project approvals, commencement certificates and occupation certificates to assess the status of projects and potential risks impacting project completion.","risk":"Regulatory approval risk on redevelopment projects"},{"note":"Explicitly named as an exposure for the Company's redevelopment projects; changes in development control regulations can alter project economics and buildable potential in Mumbai's redevelopment micro-markets.","risk":"Changes in development control regulations"},{"note":"Redevelopment carries obligations towards society members / existing occupants, including rehabilitation and transit accommodation costs that form part of attributable land and development rights costs — an obligation structurally specific to the redevelopment model.","risk":"Contractual obligations towards society members and existing occupants"},{"note":"Named as an exposure of redevelopment projects; delays in the stage of physical completion affect cost to complete and the recoverability of inventory carried against long-dated projects.","risk":"Project execution delays"},{"note":"Cost escalations are named as a risk; inventory valuation depends on management estimates of total projected construction and redevelopment costs to complete, so escalation directly compresses realisable margin.","risk":"Cost escalation on long-cycle projects"},{"note":"The determination of inventory carrying value requires management to estimate future selling prices and expected market demand; adverse movement in either would affect net realisable value.","risk":"Changing market conditions affecting selling prices and demand"},{"note":"Inventory valuation of redevelopment projects under construction and completed units held for sale was flagged as a Key Audit Matter because it involves significant management judgment and estimation uncertainty due to the long-term and complex nature of such projects, together with the materiality of the balance.","risk":"Estimation uncertainty in inventory valuation (Key Audit Matter)"},{"note":"The auditors reviewed correspondence relating to material litigations, disputes and claims with contractors, society members, regulatory authorities and other stakeholders that could affect project costs or realizability.","risk":"Litigation, disputes and claims with contractors, society members and regulatory authorities"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"MODIS","sector":"Realty","sk":null,"strategies":"Redevelopment-led growth: management states that redevelopment will remain a key driver of growth in Mumbai and that the Company is well-positioned to capitalise on it with its strong execution track record and growing project pipeline.|Disciplined asset-light strategy that management says has enabled the Company to scale efficiently while maintaining strong cash flows and operational agility.|Geographic focus on Mumbai's western suburbs and Mumbai